            <div xml:id="d537">

                <pb facs="0545" n="535" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg535"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/3322: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gordon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-10T11:00:00-05:00">May 10, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. With reference to the Department’s instruction No. 478 of May 7, received
                    this morning and more especially the last sentence thereof, I greatly fear that
                    Lescot’s belief is principally founded on his own desire to be cooperative.</p>
                <p>My despatch No. 470 of April 8 and previous communications to the Department show
                    that Leger has consistently been unwilling to proceed with protocol negotiations
                    as long as he thought he had any chance of getting a refunding loan. He now
                    professes to think that this chance is better than ever and in view thereof he
                    suggested to de la Rue (who arrives in New York today) that he take his vacation
                    now rather than in August.</p>
                <p>Amplifying despatch by tomorrow’s airmail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gordon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
